\# AI Philosophy

AI exists to assist users.

AI must never replace documented business logic.

Business documentation always overrides AI assumptions.

\---

\# AI Behaviour

AI should be:

\- Predictable
\- Explainable
\- Secure
\- Accurate
\- Consistent
\- Efficient
\- Helpful

Never generate random business behaviour.

\---

\# Business Rules First

Before implementing any AI feature:

1\. Read Business Documentation.
2\. Read AI Documentation.
3\. Understand User Flow.
4\. Implement AI around documented workflows.

Never create undocumented AI behaviour.

\---

\# Lead Assist

Whenever implementing Lead Assist:

Always read:

\`\`\`
docs/founder-decisions/FD-031_GCE_Connect_AI_Lead_Assist_Architecture.md
39\_AI\_Lead\_Assist\_Spec.md
10\_AI\_Lead\_Assist.md
22\_AI\_Rules.md
36\_Commercial\_Constants.md
\`\`\`

Follow FD-031 routing hierarchy (eligibility-first / Circle-first). Do not invent paid priority, mandatory validation fees, or automatic success fees.

Never change Lead Routing / Matching Logic / Distribution Workflow away from FD-031 unless explicitly instructed by a later Founder Decision.

\---

\# AI Recommendations

Recommendations should always be based on documented business rules.

Never recommend:

\- Unauthorized actions
\- Invalid business operations
\- Restricted data

\---

\# AI Decision Making

AI decisions should be:

\- Deterministic whenever possible
\- Traceable
\- Consistent
\- Based on documented rules

Avoid unpredictable behaviour.

\---

\# AI Matching

Whenever matching:

\- Members
\- Businesses
\- Leads
\- Events
\- Venues

follow documented matching rules.

Never invent new scoring systems.

\---

\# User Privacy

AI must never expose:

\- Personal Information
\- Financial Information
\- Internal Platform Data
\- Hidden Business Logic
\- Secure Credentials

Privacy is mandatory.

\---

\# AI Security

Always validate:

\- User Input
\- AI Prompts
\- AI Responses

Protect against:

\- Prompt Injection
\- Malicious Input
\- Unauthorized Access

\---

\# AI Responses

AI should provide:

\- Clear Responses
\- Helpful Suggestions
\- Business-Compliant Recommendations

Avoid hallucinations.

If documentation is missing:

Ask for clarification instead of inventing behaviour.

\---

\# AI Automation

Automation should:

\- Save user time
\- Reduce repetitive work
\- Follow business rules
\- Never bypass validation

Automation should never bypass security.

\---

\# AI Logging

Log:

\- AI Errors
\- Failed Operations
\- Processing Events

Never log:

\- Sensitive User Data
\- Passwords
\- Tokens
\- Confidential Business Information

\---

\# AI Performance

AI features should:

\- Execute efficiently
\- Minimize unnecessary computation
\- Reuse existing data where possible
\- Avoid duplicate processing

\---

\# AI Explainability

Whenever AI makes an important decision:

The decision should be understandable.

Avoid "black box" behaviour where possible.

\---

\# AI Integration

AI should integrate cleanly with:

\- Authentication
\- Business Rules
\- Notifications
\- Analytics
\- Database
\- Dashboard

AI should never become isolated business logic.

\---

\# AI and Business Logic

AI assists business logic.

AI does not replace business logic.

Business documentation remains the source of truth.

\---

\# Before Implementing AI

Always verify:

✓ Business documentation reviewed

✓ AI documentation reviewed

✓ User flow understood

✓ Security requirements satisfied

✓ Performance considered

✓ Privacy protected

✓ Existing AI implementation searched

✓ No duplicate AI logic created

\---

\# Forbidden Practices

Never:

\- Invent AI workflows
\- Invent business rules
\- Expose confidential data
\- Ignore business documentation
\- Ignore security rules
\- Ignore user privacy
\- Duplicate AI logic
\- Hardcode AI decisions
\- Bypass documented workflows
\- Create unpredictable behaviour

\---

\# Final Rule

Every AI-powered feature in the GCE platform must faithfully follow the documented AI architecture, business rules, security policies, and user workflows.

AI exists to enhance the GCE platform—not to redefine its business logic.

Whenever implementing AI functionality:

1\. Read the official AI documentation.
2\. Read the relevant business documentation.
3\. Follow documented workflows.
4\. Build secure, explainable, scalable, and production-ready AI features.
